    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line is emitted by `OwnerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(Owner)`. I enriched it to also log `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` while keeping the existing fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\nTo avoid duplicating derivation logic, I reused the existing util formatters \u2014 the same ones the `OwnerMapper` uses to populate the DTO:\n\n- `membershipNumber` \u2192 `MembershipNumberFormatter.format(customerCode, registrationDate)`\n- `membershipLevel` \u2192 `MembershipLevelFormatter.format(MembershipPointsFormatter.format(...))`\n\nEach is extracted into a small private helper (`membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber`) so `ownerCreated` stays a single-responsibility \"assemble and emit the record\" method rather than inlining formatting details.\n\nThe observed audit output confirms it:\n```\nAUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-21 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes, verifying the line carries both the membership number and level consistent with the owner's fetched DTO.",
